66
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,137
Wait till I get off this thing.

67
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:19,338
I'm afraid of life.

68
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,740
Gadzooks, this is horrible.

69
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:31,445
The Digimon Emperor's got his hot
little mitts on our territory.

70
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:35,697
We gotta do something or we're gonna
be slaves for the rest of our lives.

71
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,610
Right.

72
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:39,658
Facing him is like a piccolo
going up against a tuba.

73
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:42,200
Oh, I'm too tired for this.

74
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:58,797
it's about time davis let's get
moving i'm kind of worried the digimon

75
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:02,457
emperor has really started to move
faster i know one thing he's not

76
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:05,337
afraid of us or he wouldn't keep
fighting after losing all those battles

77
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:09,877
look huh this is what i'm talking
about we better take the spin out of

78
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:13,837
his wheels and fast well I'm all for
that I'm not gonna let that Brainiac

79
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:17,897
get the best of us yeah he's plotting
something big I can feel it if

80
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:21,117
I were an evil genius what would I
do he may have the brains but we have

81
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:25,259
the brawn we've got to at least take
one of those areas back from him

82
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:34,785
we're gonna teach that Digimon
Emperor a lesson once and for all

83
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:47,260
The dust is making my whiskers twitch.

84
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:49,100
This place is weird.

85
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,720
Not to mention old.

86
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:54,097
It's reminiscent of the samurai
era back in ancient Japan.

87
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:56,537
It could be a film set
from an old TV show.

88
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:58,617
My dad watched one of those last night.

89
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:01,347
I think this is definitely
the digital world.

90
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:02,850
See that?

91
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:05,040
It's a control spire.

92
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,358
That's a sure sign.

93
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,260
What was that?

94
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:11,260
Yeah, red eyes give me the creeps.

95
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,780
This looks bad.

96
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,737
What are they waiting for?

97
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,702
They already have us surrounded.

98
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:27,780
Me, my big mouth!

99
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,220
We're poor along!

100
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,973
We may look like flowers, but watch out!

101
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:38,179
Our rain of pollen will make hay
fever seem like a walk in the roses!

102
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,440
We're Mushroom Mod.

103
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,697
You definitely don't want
us in your fetchy omelet.

104
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:43,957
We may be cute as buttons,

105
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:47,277
but our Fungus Cruncher will
leave you scratching your head.

106
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,500
Rain of Pollock coming at ya!

107
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,740
Fungus Cruncher!

108
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,040
Stand back!

109
00:06:59,340 --> 00:07:01,860
You're no much for me, Cuddle Mod!

110
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:03,480
Oh, yeah?

111
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:10,620
I'm too tired to play anymore.

112
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:12,497
I think I'll take a nappy now.

113
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:13,680
Fungus Cruncher!

114
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:15,970
Puppies!

115
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:19,377
I'm not getting right.

116
